Texas League. With a team in the Texas League and the Sunland Park Racetrack, “we will be living in town and cooking with gas.”
I don't know of any two things that would give the town more publicity. There is one thing that I can't quite understand, why
go out of town and get a manager for the baseball team when we have a home town boy that
is one of the best managers in the business — Andy Cohen. He has been successful with every team that he has managed. Anyway. I hope the El Paso Club
will have the largest attendance
of any town in the league, and
I wish the promoters all the luck in the world.
—George Simpson, 619 Magoffin Ave.

